  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The Hall&ndash;H&eacute;roult process is the&nbsp;major industrial process for smelting aluminium. It involves dissolving aluminium oxide (alumina) (obtained most often from bauxite, aluminium&#39;s chief ore, through the Bayer process) in molten&nbsp;cryolite, and electrolyzing the molten salt bath, typically in a purpose-built cell.</p><p>In this process carbon electrodes are used.</p><p>The following reactions take place&nbsp;</p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>Al</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
